{
  "id": "remint-deck-items",
  "title": "Re-mint: deck items of window rows are re-minted; an e:<seq> item put into an existing deck is discarded",
  "covers": [
    "re-mint selection (SYNC.md 10.4 step 1): deck items are re-minted iff their row (deck_id, item_key) names a window row",
    "deck.item_put e:<seq> on a deck the server had: clock_ahead (its only reference exists), discarded; the key is shared by every replica that adds the same word",
    "deck.item_put n:<window note> on an existing deck, and any item of a window deck: unknown_reference, re-minted"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A creates deck D and syncs (seq 1). A's clock jumps 10 days ahead; offline, A adds word 2000001 (note + card) and puts e:2000001 into D; adds a custom note N (no entry) and puts n:N into D; creates deck D2 and puts e:2000001 into it.",
    "Meanwhile B puts another word into D (seq 2).",
    "A pushes with the clock still wrong: the two note.created, deck.created D2 and the e:2000001 put into D are clock_ahead (D exists, so that put has no missing reference); card.created, n:N into D and e:2000001 into D2 are unknown_reference.",
    "Re-mint: W = {the word's note, its card, N, D2}. n:N in D and e:2000001 in D2 write rows whose identity contains a window id: re-minted. e:2000001 in D writes the row (D, e:2000001), which any replica adding the same word to D writes too: discarded, like any edit of a row the server already has. The user adds the word to D again.",
    "A also reviewed the new card an hour after creating it (unknown_reference). It is re-minted in step 6b with a new id and reviewed_at shifted by the same delta as the creations, so it stays an hour after its card. `remint` lists the inputs; tools/validate.py recomputes the selection and the shift."
  ],
  "devices": {
